issue.body:
Jira Link: [DB-492](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-492)
### Description

When creating an index and it fails because of a duplicate key value, the index still seems to exist:
```
yugabyte=# create table t (a int);
CREATE TABLE
yugabyte=# insert into t values (1);
INSERT 0 1
yugabyte=# insert into t values (2);
INSERT 0 1
yugabyte=# insert into t values (1);
INSERT 0 1
yugabyte=# create unique index i on t(a);
ERROR:  Aborted: ERROR:  duplicate key value violates unique constraint "i"
yugabyte=# drop index i;
DROP INDEX
```
Expected behaviour, as in Postgres:
```
template1=# create table t (a int);
CREATE TABLE
template1=# insert into t values (1);
INSERT 0 1
template1=# insert into t values (1);
INSERT 0 1
template1=# create unique index i on t(a);
ERROR:  could not create unique index "i"
DETAIL:  Key (a)=(1) is duplicated.
template1=# drop index i;
ERROR:  index "i" does not exist
```
